.IX Title "AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session 3"
.TH AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session 3 "2025-11-03" "perl v5.34.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session \- Manages session revocation and tracking
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    use AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session;
\&    
\&    # Initialize session management
\&    AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->initialize(\*(AqMyRevocationTable\*(Aq);
\&    
\&    # Create session with specific ID
\&    my $session = AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->new(
\&        id => \*(Aquser\-session\-12345\*(Aq
\&    );
\&    
\&    # Create session with auto\-generated ID
\&    my $session = AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->new(
\&        autogenerate => 1,
\&        length       => 16,
\&    );
\&    
\&    # Revoke session
\&    my $success = $session\->revoke(
\&        expiry_period => 86400,
\&        reason        => \*(AqCOMPROMISED\*(Aq,
\&    );
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This class handles session creation, auto-generation, and revocation
for the secure media delivery system.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.IX Header "CLASS METHODS"
.ie n .SS "initialize($table_name, %params)"
.el .SS "initialize($table_name, \f(CW%params\fP)"
.IX Subsection "initialize($table_name, %params)"
Initialize session management with DynamoDB table.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->initialize(
\&        \*(AqMyRevocationTable\*(Aq,
\&        region => \*(Aqus\-east\-1\*(Aq
\&    );
.Ve
.SS "init_db_client(%params)"
.IX Subsection "init_db_client(%params)"
Initialize DynamoDB client.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->init_db_client(region => \*(Aqus\-east\-1\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SS "set_debug($debug)"
.IX Subsection "set_debug($debug)"
Enable or disable debug logging (class method).
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->set_debug(1);
.Ve
.SS "auto_generate($length)"
.IX Subsection "auto_generate($length)"
Auto-generate a random session \s-1ID\s0 (class method).
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $session_id = AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session\->auto_generate(16);
.Ve
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.IX Header "INSTANCE METHODS"
.SS "new(%args)"
.IX Subsection "new(%args)"
Creates a new Session instance.
.IP "\(bu" 4
id \- Session \s-1ID\s0 (optional, will be auto-generated if not provided)
.IP "\(bu" 4
autogenerate \- Whether to auto-generate session \s-1ID\s0 (default: 0)
.IP "\(bu" 4
length \- Length of auto-generated session \s-1ID\s0 (default: 12)
.IP "\(bu" 4
suspicion_score \- Suspicion score for the session (default: 0)
.SS "revoke(%args)"
.IX Subsection "revoke(%args)"
Revoke the session by adding it to the revocation table.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    my $success = $session\->revoke(
\&        expiry_period => 86400,    # seconds
\&        reason        => \*(AqCOMPROMISED\*(Aq,
\&    );
.Ve
